{"name":"Sensory Songs","type":"skill","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"healing-song-sensory","collection":"merp-rmu","source":"RMSS/RMFRP — Healing Songs","restriction":{"race":"elf"},"resultTable":"healing-songs","englishName":"Sensory Songs","compendiumSourceKey":"healing-song-sensory","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-skills","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"skills","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Chant des Sens","system":{"name":"Chant des Sens","description":"<h1>Chant des Sens (Sensory Songs)</h1><p>Chant de guérison elfique qui traite les atteintes des sens, des nerfs et certaines affections mentales.</p><p><strong>Restriction :</strong> cette Compétence est normalement réservée aux lignées elfiques. Elle est considérée comme Restreinte pour les autres peuples.</p><p><strong>Résolution :</strong> utilisez une Manœuvre de Manipulation de la Puissance. MERP-UI remplace automatiquement le résultat normal par la table spéciale des Chants de Guérison. Les modificateurs de situation, de gravité de la blessure, des chanteurs accompagnateurs et de l’affinité du patient avec les Elfes restent à appliquer dans le dialogue de Manœuvre.</p><p><strong>Modificateurs RMSS/RMFRP :</strong> situation de +30 à −70 ; nature de la maladie ou de la blessure de +30 à −70 ; jusqu’à cinq chanteurs accompagnateurs ajoutent chacun leur bonus dans le Chant concerné ; patient mortel ayant une affinité avec les Elfes : −20 ; autre mortel : −50. Ces modificateurs sont saisis dans le dialogue de Manœuvre RMU.</p>"}},"en":{"name":"Sensory Songs","system":{"name":"Sensory Songs","description":"<h1>Sensory Songs</h1><p>Elven healing song that treats injuries to the senses and nerves, as well as certain mental afflictions.</p><p><strong>Restriction:</strong> this Skill is normally reserved for Elven lineages. It is considered Restricted for other peoples.</p><p><strong>Resolution:</strong> use a Power Manipulation Maneuver. MERP-UI automatically replaces the normal result with the special Healing Songs table. Situation modifiers, injury severity, accompanying singers, and the patient’s affinity with Elves must still be entered in the Maneuver dialog.</p><p><strong>RMSS/RMFRP Modifiers:</strong> situation from +30 to −70; nature of the illness or injury from +30 to −70; up to five accompanying singers each add their bonus in the relevant Song; mortal patient with an affinity for Elves: −20; other mortal: −50. These modifiers are entered in the RMU Maneuver dialog.</p>"}}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"system":{"name":"Sensory Songs","category":"Power Manipulation","trainingGroup":null,"stat":"Em","description":"<h1>Sensory Songs</h1><p>Elven healing song that treats injuries to the senses and nerves, as well as certain mental afflictions.</p><p><strong>Restriction:</strong> this Skill is normally reserved for Elven lineages. It is considered Restricted for other peoples.</p><p><strong>Resolution:</strong> use a Power Manipulation Maneuver. MERP-UI automatically replaces the normal result with the special Healing Songs table. Situation modifiers, injury severity, accompanying singers, and the patient’s affinity with Elves must still be entered in the Maneuver dialog.</p><p><strong>RMSS/RMFRP Modifiers:</strong> situation from +30 to −70; nature of the illness or injury from +30 to −70; up to five accompanying singers each add their bonus in the relevant Song; mortal patient with an affinity for Elves: −20; other mortal: −50. These modifiers are entered in the RMU Maneuver dialog.</p>","specialization":"","attackUUID":null,"specializationType":0,"hasSpecialization":false,"fixedSpecializations":false,"specializations":[],"favorite":false,"cultureRanks":0,"ranks":0,"autoSkill":false},"_id":"BllKgWdrScp07kqN"}
{"name":"Strengthening Songs","type":"skill","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"healing-song-strengthening","collection":"merp-rmu","source":"RMSS/RMFRP — Healing Songs","restriction":{"race":"elf"},"resultTable":"healing-songs","englishName":"Strengthening Songs","compendiumSourceKey":"healing-song-strengthening","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-skills","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/khazad.json","compendiumFolderKey":"skills","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Chant de Fortification","system":{"name":"Chant de Fortification","description":"<h1>Chant de Fortification (Strengthening Songs)</h1><p>Chant elfique polyvalent capable de soutenir plusieurs formes de guérison et de fortifier l’esprit.</p><p><strong>Restriction :</strong> cette Compétence est normalement réservée aux lignées elfiques. Elle est considérée comme Restreinte pour les autres peuples.</p><p><strong>Résolution :</strong> utilisez une Manœuvre de Manipulation de la Puissance. MERP-UI remplace automatiquement le résultat normal par la table spéciale des Chants de Guérison. Les modificateurs de situation, de gravité de la blessure, des chanteurs accompagnateurs et de l’affinité du patient avec les Elfes restent à appliquer dans le dialogue de Manœuvre.</p><p><strong>Modificateurs RMSS/RMFRP :</strong> situation de +30 à −70 ; nature de la maladie ou de la blessure de +30 à −70 ; jusqu’à cinq chanteurs accompagnateurs ajoutent chacun leur bonus dans le Chant concerné ; patient mortel ayant une affinité avec les Elfes : −20 ; autre mortel : −50. Ces modificateurs sont saisis dans le dialogue de Manœuvre RMU.</p>"}},"en":{"name":"Strengthening Songs","system":{"name":"Strengthening Songs","description":"<h1>Strengthening Songs</h1><p>Versatile Elven song capable of supporting several forms of healing and strengthening the mind.</p><p><strong>Restriction:</strong> this Skill is normally reserved for Elven lineages. It is considered Restricted for other peoples.</p><p><strong>Resolution:</strong> use a Power Manipulation Maneuver. MERP-UI automatically replaces the normal result with the special Healing Songs table. Situation modifiers, injury severity, accompanying singers, and the patient’s affinity with Elves must still be entered in the Maneuver dialog.</p><p><strong>RMSS/RMFRP Modifiers:</strong> situation from +30 to −70; nature of the illness or injury from +30 to −70; up to five accompanying singers each add their bonus in the relevant Song; mortal patient with an affinity for Elves: −20; other mortal: −50. These modifiers are entered in the RMU Maneuver dialog.</p>"}}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"system":{"name":"Strengthening Songs","category":"Power Manipulation","trainingGroup":null,"stat":"Em","description":"<h1>Strengthening Songs</h1><p>Versatile Elven song capable of supporting several forms of healing and strengthening the mind.</p><p><strong>Restriction:</strong> this Skill is normally reserved for Elven lineages. It is considered Restricted for other peoples.</p><p><strong>Resolution:</strong> use a Power Manipulation Maneuver. MERP-UI automatically replaces the normal result with the special Healing Songs table. Situation modifiers, injury severity, accompanying singers, and the patient’s affinity with Elves must still be entered in the Maneuver dialog.</p><p><strong>RMSS/RMFRP Modifiers:</strong> situation from +30 to −70; nature of the illness or injury from +30 to −70; up to five accompanying singers each add their bonus in the relevant Song; mortal patient with an affinity for Elves: −20; other mortal: −50. These modifiers are entered in the RMU Maneuver dialog.</p>","specialization":"","attackUUID":null,"specializationType":0,"hasSpecialization":false,"fixedSpecializations":false,"specializations":[],"favorite":false,"cultureRanks":0,"ranks":0,"autoSkill":false},"_id":"PKHbpWPr8titisgO"}
{"name":"Healing Songs","type":"skill","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"healing-songs","collection":"merp-special-power-skills","source":"RMSS/RMFRP — Healing Songs","restriction":{"race":"elf"},"resultTable":"healing-songs","englishName":"Healing Songs","skillFamily":"Healing Songs","compendiumSourceKey":"healing-songs","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-skills","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/special-power-skills.json","compendiumFolderKey":"Skills","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Chants de Guérison","system":{"name":"Chants de Guérison","description":"<h1>Chants de Guérison (Healing Songs)</h1>\n<p>Les <strong>Chants de Guérison</strong> appartiennent aux anciennes traditions thérapeutiques des Elfes. Ils ne reposent ni sur la seule connaissance des remèdes, ni sur l’incantation d’un sort appris : le chanteur harmonise sa voix, sa volonté et la puissance d’Arda afin d’aider le corps et l’esprit du patient à retrouver leur équilibre.</p>\n<p>Cette Compétence appartient à <strong>Manipulation de la Puissance (Power Manipulation)</strong> et utilise l’<strong>Empathie (Em)</strong>. Elle est normalement réservée aux <strong>lignées elfiques</strong>. Chaque type de chant constitue une <strong>spécialisation distincte</strong> et doit être développé séparément.</p>\n<h2>Spécialisations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Chant du Sang (Blood Songs).</strong> Agit sur la circulation et l’écoulement du sang. Il peut aider à maîtriser une hémorragie ou à rétablir une circulation perturbée.</li>\n<li><strong>Chant des Os (Bone Songs).</strong> Fortifie les os et favorise la régénération partielle des fractures, y compris lorsque l’os est brisé ou fracassé.</li>\n<li><strong>Chant des Sens (Sensory Songs).</strong> Aide à réparer les atteintes des nerfs et les diminutions des facultés sensorielles. Il peut également soutenir le traitement de certaines affections mentales.</li>\n<li><strong>Chant des Muscles, Tendons et Ligaments (Muscle/Tendon/Ligament Songs).</strong> Répare, fortifie et favorise la régénération partielle des tissus mous : muscles, tendons et ligaments.</li>\n<li><strong>Chant de Purification (Cleansing Songs).</strong> Purifie le sang et les organes et aide le corps à retrouver un fonctionnement normal après une longue période d’effort, d’épuisement ou d’inactivité forcée.</li>\n<li><strong>Chant de Fortification (Strengthening Songs).</strong> Le plus polyvalent des Chants de Guérison. Il peut intervenir sur l’ensemble des affections précédentes et contribue également à fortifier l’esprit du patient.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Résolution</h2>\n<p>Un Chant de Guérison se résout par une <strong>Manœuvre de Manipulation de la Puissance</strong>. La table spéciale des Chants de Guérison remplace la table habituelle de cette catégorie. La qualité du résultat détermine si le chant échoue, aggrave l’état du patient ou permet d’appliquer un effet curatif.</p>\n<p>Lorsque le résultat autorise le choix d’un effet de guérison, le niveau maximal de cet effet dépend des <strong>rangs possédés dans la spécialisation du Chant</strong>, et non du bonus total de la Compétence. Un résultat de Réussite ou de Réussite Partielle peut permettre un effet d’un niveau allant jusqu’au nombre de rangs ; une Réussite Proche limite ce niveau à la moitié des rangs.</p>\n<h2>Modificateurs</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Situation :</strong> de <strong>+30 à −70</strong>. Une chambre calme et un chant doux favorisent la guérison ; un lieu violent, terrifiant ou chaotique peut presque rendre le chant impossible.</li>\n<li><strong>Nature de la maladie ou de la blessure :</strong> de <strong>+30 à −70</strong>. Une coupure simple est bien plus accessible qu’un poison exceptionnel ou qu’une affection particulièrement grave.</li>\n<li><strong>Chanteurs accompagnateurs :</strong> jusqu’à cinq chanteurs peuvent soutenir le chanteur principal ; chacun apporte sa propre maîtrise du chant selon les règles de la Manœuvre.</li>\n<li><strong>Patient mortel ayant une affinité avec les Elfes :</strong> pénalité de <strong>−20</strong>. Un Númenóréen Fidèle constitue l’exemple traditionnel.</li>\n<li><strong>Patient mortel sans affinité particulière avec les Elfes :</strong> pénalité de <strong>−50</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Les <strong>Noldor</strong>, dont la tradition musicale et la compréhension des arts de guérison sont particulièrement anciennes, bénéficient d’un <strong>bonus spécial de +15</strong> aux Chants de Guérison.</p>\n<h2>Table des Chants de Guérison</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Échec Spectaculaire :</strong> une dissonance s’insinue dans le chant sans être perçue avant sa conclusion. La puissance curative s’inverse et la maladie ou la blessure s’aggrave, éventuellement jusqu’à devenir mortelle. Le chanteur effectue également un jet d’Échec de Sort sans modificateur.</li>\n<li><strong>Échec Absolu :</strong> la dissonance rend cette affection impossible à guérir par chant, méditation ou sort. Il faut désormais compter sur les soins ordinaires ou les herbes.</li>\n<li><strong>Échec :</strong> cette affection dépasse les capacités du chanteur. D’autres méthodes ou d’autres chanteurs peuvent encore être essayés.</li>\n<li><strong>Événement Inhabituel :</strong> l’association du patient, du chant et des chanteurs produit une magie rare. Le chanteur principal peut interrompre le chant — tous les participants subissent alors un jet sur la table de Force des Échecs de Sort — ou poursuivre, avec des conséquences entièrement inhabituelles déterminées par le MJ.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Partielle :</strong> le chant agit difficilement. Le chanteur peut choisir un effet de guérison approprié dont le niveau ne dépasse pas ses rangs dans cette spécialisation, ou laisser le MJ déterminer l’effet.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Inhabituelle :</strong> le chant guérit et fortifie le patient au-delà de ce que la maîtrise normale du chanteur permettrait. Le résultat exact relève du MJ.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Proche :</strong> le chant agit, mais avec une puissance limitée. L’effet de guérison choisi ne peut dépasser la moitié des rangs du chanteur dans cette spécialisation.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite :</strong> le chant produit pleinement son effet. Le chanteur peut choisir un effet de guérison approprié dont le niveau ne dépasse pas ses rangs dans cette spécialisation.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Absolue :</strong> des paroles de pouvoir se mêlent au chant et l’affection est entièrement guérie.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>MERP-UI :</strong> la table spéciale ci-dessus est appliquée automatiquement lors du jet de la Compétence.</p>"}},"en":{"name":"Healing Songs","system":{"name":"Healing Songs","description":"<h1>Healing Songs</h1>\n<p><strong>Healing Songs</strong> belong to the ancient therapeutic traditions of the Elves. They rely neither on knowledge of remedies alone nor on the incantation of a learned spell: the singer harmonizes voice, will, and the power of Arda to help restore balance to the patient's body and spirit.</p>\n<p>This Skill belongs to <strong>Power Manipulation</strong> and uses <strong>Empathy (Em)</strong>. It is normally reserved for <strong>Elven lineages</strong>. Each type of song is a <strong>distinct specialization</strong> and must be developed separately.</p>\n<h2>Specializations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Blood Songs.</strong> Acts upon circulation and blood flow. It can help control bleeding or restore impaired circulation.</li>\n<li><strong>Bone Songs.</strong> Strengthens bones and promotes partial regeneration of fractures, including broken or shattered bones.</li>\n<li><strong>Sensory Songs.</strong> Helps repair nerve injuries and diminished sensory faculties. It can also support treatment of certain mental afflictions.</li>\n<li><strong>Muscle/Tendon/Ligament Songs.</strong> Repairs, strengthens, and promotes partial regeneration of soft tissue: muscles, tendons, and ligaments.</li>\n<li><strong>Cleansing Songs.</strong> Purifies the blood and organs and helps the body return to normal function after a long period of exertion, exhaustion, or forced inactivity.</li>\n<li><strong>Strengthening Songs.</strong> The most versatile of the Healing Songs. It can address all the preceding afflictions and also helps strengthen the patient's mind.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Resolution</h2>\n<p>A Healing Song is resolved with a <strong>Power Manipulation Maneuver</strong>. The special Healing Songs table replaces the normal table for this category. The quality of the result determines whether the song fails, worsens the patient's condition, or allows a healing effect to be applied.</p>\n<p>When the result permits the choice of a healing effect, the maximum level of that effect depends on the <strong>ranks possessed in the Song specialization</strong>, not on the Skill's total bonus. A Success or Partial Success can allow an effect whose level is no greater than the number of ranks; a Near Success limits this level to half the ranks.</p>\n<h2>Modifiers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Situation:</strong> from <strong>+30 to −70</strong>. A quiet room and gentle singing favor healing; a violent, terrifying, or chaotic place can make the song almost impossible.</li>\n<li><strong>Nature of the disease or injury:</strong> from <strong>+30 to −70</strong>. A simple cut is far easier to treat than an exceptional poison or a particularly severe affliction.</li>\n<li><strong>Accompanying singers:</strong> up to five singers may support the lead singer; each contributes their own mastery of the song according to the Maneuver rules.</li>\n<li><strong>Mortal patient with an affinity for Elves:</strong> <strong>−20</strong> penalty. A Faithful Númenórean is the traditional example.</li>\n<li><strong>Mortal patient without any particular affinity for Elves:</strong> <strong>−50</strong> penalty.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <strong>Noldor</strong>, whose musical tradition and understanding of the healing arts are particularly ancient, receive a <strong>special +15 bonus</strong> to Healing Songs.</p>\n<h2>Healing Songs Table</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Spectacular Failure:</strong> a dissonance enters the song without being noticed before its conclusion. The healing power reverses and the illness or injury worsens, possibly becoming fatal. The singer also makes an unmodified Spell Failure roll.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Failure:</strong> the dissonance makes this affliction impossible to heal through song, meditation, or spell. Ordinary care or herbs must now be relied upon.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure:</strong> this affliction is beyond the singer's ability. Other methods or other singers may still be tried.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Event:</strong> the combination of patient, song, and singers produces rare magic. The lead singer may stop the song—in which case all participants make a roll on the Spell Failure Severity table—or continue, with wholly unusual consequences determined by the GM.</li>\n<li><strong>Partial Success:</strong> the song works with difficulty. The singer may choose an appropriate healing effect whose level does not exceed their ranks in that specialization, or let the GM determine the effect.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Success:</strong> the song heals and strengthens the patient beyond what the singer's normal mastery would allow. The exact result is determined by the GM.</li>\n<li><strong>Near Success:</strong> the song works, but with limited power. The chosen healing effect may not exceed half the singer's ranks in that specialization.</li>\n<li><strong>Success:</strong> the song produces its full effect. The singer may choose an appropriate healing effect whose level does not exceed their ranks in that specialization.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Success:</strong> words of power mingle with the song and the affliction is completely healed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>MERP-UI:</strong> the special table above is applied automatically when the Skill is rolled.</p>"}}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"system":{"name":"Healing Songs","category":"Power Manipulation","trainingGroup":null,"stat":"Em","description":"<h1>Healing Songs</h1>\n<p><strong>Healing Songs</strong> belong to the ancient therapeutic traditions of the Elves. They rely neither on knowledge of remedies alone nor on the incantation of a learned spell: the singer harmonizes voice, will, and the power of Arda to help restore balance to the patient's body and spirit.</p>\n<p>This Skill belongs to <strong>Power Manipulation</strong> and uses <strong>Empathy (Em)</strong>. It is normally reserved for <strong>Elven lineages</strong>. Each type of song is a <strong>distinct specialization</strong> and must be developed separately.</p>\n<h2>Specializations</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Blood Songs.</strong> Acts upon circulation and blood flow. It can help control bleeding or restore impaired circulation.</li>\n<li><strong>Bone Songs.</strong> Strengthens bones and promotes partial regeneration of fractures, including broken or shattered bones.</li>\n<li><strong>Sensory Songs.</strong> Helps repair nerve injuries and diminished sensory faculties. It can also support treatment of certain mental afflictions.</li>\n<li><strong>Muscle/Tendon/Ligament Songs.</strong> Repairs, strengthens, and promotes partial regeneration of soft tissue: muscles, tendons, and ligaments.</li>\n<li><strong>Cleansing Songs.</strong> Purifies the blood and organs and helps the body return to normal function after a long period of exertion, exhaustion, or forced inactivity.</li>\n<li><strong>Strengthening Songs.</strong> The most versatile of the Healing Songs. It can address all the preceding afflictions and also helps strengthen the patient's mind.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Resolution</h2>\n<p>A Healing Song is resolved with a <strong>Power Manipulation Maneuver</strong>. The special Healing Songs table replaces the normal table for this category. The quality of the result determines whether the song fails, worsens the patient's condition, or allows a healing effect to be applied.</p>\n<p>When the result permits the choice of a healing effect, the maximum level of that effect depends on the <strong>ranks possessed in the Song specialization</strong>, not on the Skill's total bonus. A Success or Partial Success can allow an effect whose level is no greater than the number of ranks; a Near Success limits this level to half the ranks.</p>\n<h2>Modifiers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Situation:</strong> from <strong>+30 to −70</strong>. A quiet room and gentle singing favor healing; a violent, terrifying, or chaotic place can make the song almost impossible.</li>\n<li><strong>Nature of the disease or injury:</strong> from <strong>+30 to −70</strong>. A simple cut is far easier to treat than an exceptional poison or a particularly severe affliction.</li>\n<li><strong>Accompanying singers:</strong> up to five singers may support the lead singer; each contributes their own mastery of the song according to the Maneuver rules.</li>\n<li><strong>Mortal patient with an affinity for Elves:</strong> <strong>−20</strong> penalty. A Faithful Númenórean is the traditional example.</li>\n<li><strong>Mortal patient without any particular affinity for Elves:</strong> <strong>−50</strong> penalty.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The <strong>Noldor</strong>, whose musical tradition and understanding of the healing arts are particularly ancient, receive a <strong>special +15 bonus</strong> to Healing Songs.</p>\n<h2>Healing Songs Table</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Spectacular Failure:</strong> a dissonance enters the song without being noticed before its conclusion. The healing power reverses and the illness or injury worsens, possibly becoming fatal. The singer also makes an unmodified Spell Failure roll.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Failure:</strong> the dissonance makes this affliction impossible to heal through song, meditation, or spell. Ordinary care or herbs must now be relied upon.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure:</strong> this affliction is beyond the singer's ability. Other methods or other singers may still be tried.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Event:</strong> the combination of patient, song, and singers produces rare magic. The lead singer may stop the song—in which case all participants make a roll on the Spell Failure Severity table—or continue, with wholly unusual consequences determined by the GM.</li>\n<li><strong>Partial Success:</strong> the song works with difficulty. The singer may choose an appropriate healing effect whose level does not exceed their ranks in that specialization, or let the GM determine the effect.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Success:</strong> the song heals and strengthens the patient beyond what the singer's normal mastery would allow. The exact result is determined by the GM.</li>\n<li><strong>Near Success:</strong> the song works, but with limited power. The chosen healing effect may not exceed half the singer's ranks in that specialization.</li>\n<li><strong>Success:</strong> the song produces its full effect. The singer may choose an appropriate healing effect whose level does not exceed their ranks in that specialization.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Success:</strong> words of power mingle with the song and the affliction is completely healed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>MERP-UI:</strong> the special table above is applied automatically when the Skill is rolled.</p>","specialization":"","attackUUID":null,"specializationType":0,"hasSpecialization":true,"fixedSpecializations":true,"specializations":["Blood Songs","Bone Songs","Sensory Songs","Muscle/Tendon/Ligament Songs","Cleansing Songs","Strengthening Songs"],"favorite":false,"cultureRanks":0,"ranks":0,"autoSkill":false},"_id":"4g4tpSiDNsiHPLm4"}
{"name":"Yavanna's Song","type":"skill","img":"systems/rmu/icons/svg/iron_crown_w.svg","effects":[],"ownership":{"default":0},"flags":{"merp-ui":{"key":"yavannas-song","collection":"merp-special-power-skills","source":"RMSS/RMFRP — Yavanna's Song","restriction":{"cultures":["Sindar","Elfes sylvains"]},"resultTable":"yavannas-song","englishName":"Yavanna's Song","compendiumSourceKey":"yavannas-song","compendiumPack":"merp-rmu-skills","compendiumSourceFile":"data/merp-rmu/special-power-skills.json","compendiumFolderKey":"Skills","compendiumBuildLanguage":"en","compendiumLocalizations":{"fr":{"name":"Chant de Yavanna","system":{"name":"Chant de Yavanna","description":"<h1>Chant de Yavanna (Yavanna’s Song)</h1>\n<p>Le <strong>Chant de Yavanna</strong> est un art elfique destiné à éveiller et magnifier les vertus naturelles des herbes. La voix ne remplace pas la plante : elle s’accorde à sa nature et en renforce la vitalité, la conservation ou la puissance. À son plus haut degré, le chant peut même transformer une plante vivante en une variété nouvelle.</p>\n<p>Cette Compétence appartient à <strong>Manipulation de la Puissance (Power Manipulation)</strong> et utilise l’<strong>Empathie (Em)</strong>. Elle est réservée aux <strong>Sindar</strong> et aux <strong>Elfes sylvains</strong> dans notre adaptation.</p>\n<h2>Un chant de chœurs</h2>\n<p>Le Chant de Yavanna atteint sa pleine puissance lorsqu’il est chanté <strong>en symphonie</strong>. Sa structure comporte plusieurs vers qui doivent être échangés en réponse entre deux chœurs. Un chanteur isolé peut tenter le chant, mais l’intervention de plusieurs voix en renforce considérablement l’harmonie.</p>\n<p>Chez les Elfes Gris et les Elfes des Bois, cet art est traditionnellement particulièrement répandu parmi les guérisseuses. Certaines de ses applications rituelles sont réservées aux femmes, notamment la récolte du blé de Yavanna destiné au <strong>lembas</strong>, accomplie sous la conduite de la <em>besain</em>, reine ou femme de plus haut rang de la communauté.</p>\n<h2>Résolution</h2>\n<p>Le Chant de Yavanna se résout par une <strong>Manœuvre de Manipulation de la Puissance</strong>. Sa table spéciale remplace la table habituelle. La réussite agit sur une herbe précise : elle peut prolonger sa durée de conservation, doubler son efficacité immédiate ou, dans des circonstances exceptionnelles, modifier sa nature même.</p>\n<p>Les altérations produites par un mauvais chant ne sont pas toujours immédiatement visibles. Lorsque la table l’exige, une Manœuvre réussie d’<strong>Herboristerie (Herbalism)</strong> est nécessaire pour comprendre que la plante a perdu sa vertu, qu’elle a été transformée ou qu’elle est devenue dangereuse.</p>\n<h2>Modificateurs</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Chanteuse :</strong> bonus de <strong>+5</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Chaque chanteur supplémentaire :</strong> bonus de <strong>+5</strong>, jusqu’à un maximum de dix chanteurs supplémentaires.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Table du Chant de Yavanna</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Maladresse / Échec Spectaculaire :</strong> une dissonance inverse la puissance de l’herbe, qui agit désormais comme un poison. Une Manœuvre réussie d’Herboristerie est nécessaire pour remarquer cette inversion.</li>\n<li><strong>Échec Absolu :</strong> la dissonance dissipe la vertu de l’herbe. Une Manœuvre réussie d’Herboristerie est nécessaire pour constater qu’elle est devenue sans effet.</li>\n<li><strong>Échec :</strong> le chant n’altère pas la plante. Un autre chanteur peut tenter de reprendre le chant.</li>\n<li><strong>Événement Inhabituel :</strong> la combinaison particulière de la plante et du chant modifie sa nature d’une manière déterminée par le MJ. Une Manœuvre réussie d’Herboristerie révèle qu’une altération a eu lieu, sans nécessairement en dévoiler l’effet exact.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Partielle :</strong> l’herbe se conserve <strong>trois fois plus longtemps</strong> que normalement.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Inhabituelle :</strong> si elle n’a pas encore été cueillie, la plante évolue vers une <strong>nouvelle variété</strong> déterminée par le MJ ; convenablement entretenue, cette variété peut se reproduire. Si la plante était déjà cueillie, traitez le résultat comme un Événement Inhabituel.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Proche :</strong> l’herbe se conserve <strong>trois fois plus longtemps</strong> et son efficacité est <strong>doublée</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite :</strong> l’herbe se conserve <strong>quatre fois plus longtemps</strong> et son efficacité est <strong>doublée</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Réussite Absolue :</strong> les paroles de pouvoir exaltent profondément la vertu naturelle de la plante. Le chanteur choisit l’un des deux effets appropriés : l’herbe se conserve <strong>vingt fois plus longtemps</strong>, ou sa vertu immédiate est doublée. Une plante qui soigne normalement une fracture pourrait ainsi permettre de traiter un os fracassé.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>MERP-UI :</strong> la table spéciale ci-dessus est appliquée automatiquement lors du jet de la Compétence.</p>"}},"en":{"name":"Yavanna's Song","system":{"name":"Yavanna's Song","description":"<h1>Yavanna's Song</h1>\n<p><strong>Yavanna's Song</strong> is an Elven art intended to awaken and magnify the natural virtues of herbs. The voice does not replace the plant: it attunes itself to the plant's nature and strengthens its vitality, preservation, or potency. At its highest level, the song can even transform a living plant into a new variety.</p>\n<p>This Skill belongs to <strong>Power Manipulation</strong> and uses <strong>Empathy (Em)</strong>. In our adaptation, it is reserved for the <strong>Sindar</strong> and <strong>Silvan Elves</strong>.</p>\n<h2>A Song of Choirs</h2>\n<p>Yavanna's Song reaches its full power when sung <strong>in symphony</strong>. Its structure contains several verses that must be exchanged responsively between two choirs. A lone singer may attempt the song, but several voices greatly strengthen its harmony.</p>\n<p>Among the Grey Elves and Wood-elves, this art is traditionally especially common among healers. Some of its ritual applications are reserved for women, notably the harvesting of Yavanna's grain used for <strong>lembas</strong>, performed under the direction of the <em>besain</em>, the queen or highest-ranking woman of the community.</p>\n<h2>Resolution</h2>\n<p>Yavanna's Song is resolved with a <strong>Power Manipulation Maneuver</strong>. Its special table replaces the normal one. A successful result affects one specific herb: it may extend its preservation time, double its immediate effectiveness, or, in exceptional circumstances, alter its very nature.</p>\n<p>Changes caused by a poor song are not always immediately visible. When the table requires it, a successful <strong>Herbalism</strong> Maneuver is needed to determine that the plant has lost its virtue, been transformed, or become dangerous.</p>\n<h2>Modifiers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Lead singer:</strong> <strong>+5</strong> bonus.</li>\n<li><strong>Each additional singer:</strong> <strong>+5</strong> bonus, up to a maximum of ten additional singers.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Yavanna's Song Table</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Blunder / Spectacular Failure:</strong> a dissonance reverses the herb's power, causing it to act as a poison. A successful Herbalism Maneuver is required to notice this inversion.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Failure:</strong> the dissonance dissipates the herb's virtue. A successful Herbalism Maneuver is required to determine that it has become ineffective.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure:</strong> the song does not alter the plant. Another singer may attempt the song.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Event:</strong> the particular combination of plant and song alters its nature in a way determined by the GM. A successful Herbalism Maneuver reveals that a change has occurred without necessarily revealing its exact effect.</li>\n<li><strong>Partial Success:</strong> the herb keeps for <strong>three times longer</strong> than normal.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Success:</strong> if it has not yet been gathered, the plant evolves into a <strong>new variety</strong> determined by the GM; if properly tended, this variety may reproduce. If the plant had already been gathered, treat the result as an Unusual Event.</li>\n<li><strong>Near Success:</strong> the herb keeps for <strong>three times longer</strong> and its effectiveness is <strong>doubled</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Success:</strong> the herb keeps for <strong>four times longer</strong> and its effectiveness is <strong>doubled</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Success:</strong> words of power profoundly exalt the plant's natural virtue. The singer chooses one of two appropriate effects: the herb keeps for <strong>twenty times longer</strong>, or its immediate virtue is doubled. A plant that would normally heal a fracture could thus allow a shattered bone to be treated.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>MERP-UI:</strong> the special table above is applied automatically when the Skill is rolled.</p>"}}},"compendiumAgeVariants":null,"compendiumFolderPath":{"fr":[],"en":[]},"compendiumFolderKeyPath":[],"compendiumResolverBacked":false}},"system":{"name":"Yavanna's Song","category":"Power Manipulation","trainingGroup":null,"stat":"Em","description":"<h1>Yavanna's Song</h1>\n<p><strong>Yavanna's Song</strong> is an Elven art intended to awaken and magnify the natural virtues of herbs. The voice does not replace the plant: it attunes itself to the plant's nature and strengthens its vitality, preservation, or potency. At its highest level, the song can even transform a living plant into a new variety.</p>\n<p>This Skill belongs to <strong>Power Manipulation</strong> and uses <strong>Empathy (Em)</strong>. In our adaptation, it is reserved for the <strong>Sindar</strong> and <strong>Silvan Elves</strong>.</p>\n<h2>A Song of Choirs</h2>\n<p>Yavanna's Song reaches its full power when sung <strong>in symphony</strong>. Its structure contains several verses that must be exchanged responsively between two choirs. A lone singer may attempt the song, but several voices greatly strengthen its harmony.</p>\n<p>Among the Grey Elves and Wood-elves, this art is traditionally especially common among healers. Some of its ritual applications are reserved for women, notably the harvesting of Yavanna's grain used for <strong>lembas</strong>, performed under the direction of the <em>besain</em>, the queen or highest-ranking woman of the community.</p>\n<h2>Resolution</h2>\n<p>Yavanna's Song is resolved with a <strong>Power Manipulation Maneuver</strong>. Its special table replaces the normal one. A successful result affects one specific herb: it may extend its preservation time, double its immediate effectiveness, or, in exceptional circumstances, alter its very nature.</p>\n<p>Changes caused by a poor song are not always immediately visible. When the table requires it, a successful <strong>Herbalism</strong> Maneuver is needed to determine that the plant has lost its virtue, been transformed, or become dangerous.</p>\n<h2>Modifiers</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Lead singer:</strong> <strong>+5</strong> bonus.</li>\n<li><strong>Each additional singer:</strong> <strong>+5</strong> bonus, up to a maximum of ten additional singers.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Yavanna's Song Table</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Blunder / Spectacular Failure:</strong> a dissonance reverses the herb's power, causing it to act as a poison. A successful Herbalism Maneuver is required to notice this inversion.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Failure:</strong> the dissonance dissipates the herb's virtue. A successful Herbalism Maneuver is required to determine that it has become ineffective.</li>\n<li><strong>Failure:</strong> the song does not alter the plant. Another singer may attempt the song.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Event:</strong> the particular combination of plant and song alters its nature in a way determined by the GM. A successful Herbalism Maneuver reveals that a change has occurred without necessarily revealing its exact effect.</li>\n<li><strong>Partial Success:</strong> the herb keeps for <strong>three times longer</strong> than normal.</li>\n<li><strong>Unusual Success:</strong> if it has not yet been gathered, the plant evolves into a <strong>new variety</strong> determined by the GM; if properly tended, this variety may reproduce. If the plant had already been gathered, treat the result as an Unusual Event.</li>\n<li><strong>Near Success:</strong> the herb keeps for <strong>three times longer</strong> and its effectiveness is <strong>doubled</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Success:</strong> the herb keeps for <strong>four times longer</strong> and its effectiveness is <strong>doubled</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Absolute Success:</strong> words of power profoundly exalt the plant's natural virtue. The singer chooses one of two appropriate effects: the herb keeps for <strong>twenty times longer</strong>, or its immediate virtue is doubled. A plant that would normally heal a fracture could thus allow a shattered bone to be treated.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>MERP-UI:</strong> the special table above is applied automatically when the Skill is rolled.</p>","specialization":"","attackUUID":null,"specializationType":0,"hasSpecialization":false,"fixedSpecializations":false,"specializations":[],"favorite":false,"cultureRanks":0,"ranks":0,"autoSkill":false},"_id":"Wsg0ZZudXyFcpLNt"}
